B.aO0=new A.kI("Liber et Libri is a free library of classic books with a focus (speed-reading) mode. Everything you read is stored only on this device. There are no accounts and no tracking.",null)
B.aO1=new A.kI("Speed-read mode shows one word at a time. It is great for focus and for getting through a chapter, but research shows that reading much faster usually costs some comprehension. Pick a pace that feels comfortable and switch back to the page whenever you like.",null)
B.aO2=new A.kI("Pride and Prejudice: plates by Hugh Thomson (George Allen, 1894) and C. E. Brock (Macmillan, 1895). Frankenstein: frontispiece and title-page vignette by Theodor von Holst, engraved by W. Chevalier (Colburn & Bentley, 1831). All are public domain; scans from Wikimedia Commons. Full per-plate sources are listed in the app\u2019s attribution file.",null)
B.aO3=new A.kI("Definitions come from Webster\u2019s Revised Unabridged Dictionary (G. & C. Merriam Co., 1913), a public-domain work, via the Project Gutenberg text (gutenberg.org/ebooks/29765) as parsed by the WebstersEnglishDictionary project on GitHub. Definitions are shortened to their first senses; being from 1913, they reflect the usage and attitudes of their time.",null)
B.aO4=new A.kI("All books come from Standard Ebooks (standardebooks.org), a volunteer project that produces carefully proofread, beautifully formatted editions of public-domain works.",null)
